      "slug": "joan-of-arc-painting",
      "title": "Joan of Arc (painting)",
      "year": 1879,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/JoanOfArcLarge.jpeg",
      "imageWidth": 3612,
      "imageHeight": 3250,
      "story": "Joan of Arc is an oil on canvas painting by Jules Bastien-Lepage, from 1879. It was exhibited at the Exposition Universelle in Paris in 1889. It is held in the Metropolitan Museum of Art, in New York.",
      "facts": [
        "Joan of Arc, a national hero of France following the Hundred Years' War, became an increasingly important figure in the French cultural scene during the 1870s and 1880s, following the country's defeat in the Franco-Prussian War.",
        "That conflict had seen Prussia annex the eastern part of Lorraine, the region both Joan of Arc and Bastien-Lepage were born in."
      ],
