      "slug": "village-love",
      "title": "Village Love",
      "year": 1882,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/Bastien_Lepage_LAmour_au_Village_2.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 825,
      "imageHeight": 900,
      "story": "Village Love or The Village Lovers is an oil on canvas painting by Jules Bastien-Lepage, from 1882. It is held at the Pushkin Museum, in Moscow.",
      "facts": [
        "It was acquired in 1885 by Russian art patron Sergei Tretyakov at the posthumous sale of the artist's works at Georges Petit's gallery, in Paris.",
