      "imageWidth": 3572,
      "imageHeight": 3774,
      "story": "Le Père Jacques  is an oil on canvas painting by the French painter Jules Bastien-Lepage, created in 1881. Exhibited at the Salon of 1882, in Paris, the work is now held at the Milwaukee Art Museum.",
      "facts": [
        "The painting is a genre scene which represents an old man carrying a heavy load of wood on his back, in a forest where a little girl precedes him, busy picking tiny flowers.",
